# TUI

Launch shows `WelcomeScreen` (wordmark, then profiles). Settings can skip it with a startup profile. After that, five modes live in one `AppShell`. Search is home. The welcome screen is a full `Screen`, not a sixth mode. Help and prompts are `ModalScreen`.

```
Search  Queue  Playlists  Profiles  Settings              <user>
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 mode body (search table / queue / playlists / ...)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
▶ Title - Artist
████░░░░  01:45 / 03:18                         ▮▮▮▮▯▯  80%
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
enter play   a queue   space pause   / search   ? help
```

- Now-playing stays in the shell. Modes do not cover it.
- At width >= 110, a Queue pane docks beside the active mode (hidden when Queue is the mode).
- Wordmark is the 3-line box-drawing `YTMUSIC` plus `T U I` (one line when height < 24).

**Global:** `1`-`5` modes, `Tab` / `Shift+Tab` cycle, `Shift+H` / `Shift+L` cycle when not in an Input, `/` search field, `Space` play/pause (types a space in an Input), `+` `=` `-` volume, `>` `<` queue skip, `?` help, `q` quit when not in an Input, `Ctrl+q` always quits, `Esc` closes a modal (does not change mode). `/` or `i` from a song list focuses the search query. `Esc` blurs search to results when present, or the search mode when results are empty (never leaves focus empty).

**Welcome:** `Enter` select, `n` new profile, `q` quit. Player keys do nothing until the screen dismisses.

**Lists:** `j`/`k` or arrows, `g`/`G` first/last, `Ctrl+d`/`Ctrl+u` half-page, `Ctrl+f`/`Ctrl+b` page, `Enter` play (playlist Enter loads the queue), `a` append, `A` add to playlist, `d` remove queue item or playlist track, `n` new playlist or profile, `s` save settings.

Colors live in `theme.py` and `app.tcss` only. No hex in Python widgets.

- Background `#0B0E14`, surface `#141A22`, panel `#1B2330`
- Foreground `#E8EDF4`, muted `#8B95A5`
- Primary `#E0B15A`, focus `#6EC8C0`, playing `#3DDC97`
- Warning `#D89B4A`, error `#E06C75`, border `#2A3444`

Focus: `border: tall $accent`. Playing row: mint `♫`. Minimum 80x24; now-playing is one line when height < 24.

Use `self.notify(..., severity=...)`. Do not bind a key that only `bell()`s. Empty lists show a message.
